---
description: Fix Strapi Cloud image uploads when /api/upload returns 500 — use migration base64 upload for directory collection types
globs: scripts/push-*-to-cloud.js, scripts/push-collection-images-migration.js, scripts/finish-collection-images-on-cloud.js, scripts/lib/cloud-image-migration-config.js, src/index.js, documentation/front_end_based_collection_types_import/production_cloud_data_push/**/*
alwaysApply: false
---

- **When to use this fix**
  - Content is already on Strapi Cloud (text + tenant links OK) but **images are missing** or all cards show the same placeholder.
  - `POST /api/upload` on Cloud returns **HTTP 500** (broken S3 / `InvalidAccessKeyId`) or migration endpoints are required.
  - Local images exist under `public/uploads/` from phase-A import.

- **Canonical solution (June 2026 — proven on Catholicate)**
  - **Do not rely on** Cloud `POST /api/upload` when S3 credentials are invalid.
  - Use **`POST /api/migration/fix-published`** with `uploadMedia` (base64) + `linkCollectionImages` — implemented in [src/index.js](mdc:src/index.js).
  - Generic scripts:
    - [scripts/push-collection-images-migration.js](mdc:scripts/push-collection-images-migration.js)
    - [scripts/finish-collection-images-on-cloud.js](mdc:scripts/finish-collection-images-on-cloud.js)
    - Registry: [scripts/lib/cloud-image-migration-config.js](mdc:scripts/lib/cloud-image-migration-config.js)

- **Standard command (any registered collection)**
  ```bash
  npm run finish:collection-images-on-cloud -- --collection=catholicate --tenant-id=tenant_demo_002
  ```
  - Replace `catholicate` with: `ecumenical`, `saints`, `publications`, `theological-seminaries`, `holy-synod`, `institutions`, `training`, `kalpana-editions`, `kalpana-documents`.
  - **After every Strapi Cloud deploy**, re-run images for affected types (batch): `npm run finish:all-collection-images-on-cloud -- --tenant-id=tenant_demo_002`
  - **Stop local Strapi dev server** before running (embedded Strapi reads local DB).
  - Requires migration code **deployed on Cloud** (`git push` or `npx strapi deploy --force`).

- **Prerequisites**
  - `.env`: `STRAPI_CLOUD_URL`, `STRAPI_CLOUD_API_TOKEN` (Full Access). Use `dotenv` with `override: true` if shell env sets `STRAPI_CLOUD_URL` to localhost.
  - Phase A local import complete; content already pushed to Cloud via `push:*-to-cloud`.
  - `STRAPI_IMPORT_NODE_ENV=staging` or scripts default to `staging` for local DB.

- **Workflow order**
  1. Push **content + tenant** first: `npm run push:<section>-to-cloud -- --tenant-id=tenant_demo_002`
  2. Deploy code if migration endpoint not live (probe returns `"articles array is required."` without `uploadMedia` hint).
  3. Push **images**: `npm run finish:collection-images-on-cloud -- --collection=<key> --tenant-id=tenant_demo_002`
  4. Verify REST: `populate[image]=*` + `filters[tenant][tenantId][$eq]=tenant_demo_002` — each entry should have a **distinct** `image.url`.

- **Adding a new collection type**
  1. Add entry to [cloud-image-migration-config.js](mdc:scripts/lib/cloud-image-migration-config.js) (`uid`, `table`, `tenantLinkTable`, `entryIdCol`, `restPlural`).
  2. Document in `production_cloud_data_push/<section>-production-cloud-push-prd.html` § **Cloud image upload fix**.
  3. Add AI prompt block: *"Upload the Cloud images for [Section] using the Cloud image migration fix."*

- **AI invocation phrase (user → agent)**
  - *"Upload the Cloud images for [collection] using the Cloud image migration fix."*
  - Agent reads: [cloud-image-upload-migration-fix.html](mdc:documentation/front_end_based_collection_types_import/production_cloud_data_push/cloud-image-upload-migration-fix.html) + per-type PRD § Cloud image upload fix.
  - Agent runs `finish:collection-images-on-cloud` with the matching `--collection` key; does not ask user to run scripts.

- **Alternative (when S3 is fixed on Cloud)**
  - Set valid `AWS_*` in Strapi Cloud → Settings → Variables.
  - Re-run: `npm run push:<section>-to-cloud -- --tenant-id=tenant_demo_002 --images-only`

- **References**
  - Master doc: [cloud-image-upload-migration-fix.html](mdc:documentation/front_end_based_collection_types_import/production_cloud_data_push/cloud-image-upload-migration-fix.html)
